.Dd March 12, 2026
.Dt PS2 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ps2
.Nd i8042-compatible PS/2 controller driver
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device ps2"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver initializes and manages an i8042-compatible PS/2 controller.
It provides the controller-side bring-up for the keyboard on port 1 and,
when present, the auxiliary device on port 2.
.Pp
The controller initialization sequence:
.Bl -enum
.It
Disables both ports.
.It
Flushes stale output-buffer bytes.
.It
Reads and rewrites the controller configuration byte with interrupts masked
and translation enabled.
.It
Runs the controller self-test and retries it once before failing.
.It
Detects dual-channel capability and tests each interface.
.It
Re-enables working ports and restores IRQ delivery.
.It
If port 2 is present, resets the auxiliary device and enables data reporting.
.El
.Pp
If the second port test fails, the driver falls back to single-channel mode
and continues with keyboard-only operation.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/sys/drivers/input/ps2.c"
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/ps2.c
Controller implementation.
.It Pa /sys/drivers/input/ps2.h
Register definitions and controller constants.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr keyboard 4 ,
.Xr mouse 4
